<title>AUSTRIA: Tyrolean Air to invest 800 mln ATS in fleet.</title>
<headline>Tyrolean Air to invest 800 mln ATS in fleet.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyrolean Airways, majority-owned by Austrian Airlines, said it would invest up to 800 million schillings until the end of the year to expand its fleet of regional aircraft.</p>
<p>The company said it would add two 50-seat Canadair Regional Jets and three Dash-8/300 to its fleet. After the sale of three older planes Tyrolean's fleet would consist of 26 aircraft, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Austrian Air, the country's flag carrier, holds 52.85 percent of Tyrolean's shares.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
